  data: {
    LLM: 'Focus on reducing hand value. Meld early to get cards out, but remember that table melds help opponents manipulate. Knock when you have a low hand.\n\nTrack which cards have been played to estimate what opponents hold. Plan manipulation moves in advance - visualize how you can rearrange table melds before your turn. Use jokers strategically.\n\nControl the pace by deciding when to meld. Sometimes holding cards is better than helping opponents with table melds. Complex manipulation chains can empty your hand in one turn. Knock timing is crucial - too early and someone might undercut; too late and opponent may go out completely.',
